// P7-IN2 (industries 5.3, 5.3a): the tier plans, one for each upgrade of a stage kind (the stage panel's Upgrade button places the next tier's plan beside the stage's premises as ghosts; the tier changes when its pieces are built).
// Each is an open-air plan (open_air: pieces on bare ground, no door asked of it) holding the pieces the tier is recognised from (chains.jsonc, recognise) and, where 5.3a asks for more hand-built work, more of the stage's own hand-built piece
// (rails, runways, tables); the bills are tuned to that table at the candidate prices (labour 30 a worker-hour, rope left out; IN-27 checks every plan within 20%). The powered plans hold the machines and their shafts; the wheel and the leat are the player's.
